From 502081446fff86e85608539d599b40cf7d927fe7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AmirSalahY <hello@noury.ch>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 16:10:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/25] fix(ui): Esc dismisses again; hold the menu after
 Enter; lastUsed ordering
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Esc had stopped working entirely. readline reports the bare ESC byte as
{ name: "escape", meta: true } — ESC is also the escape-sequence introducer, so
the flag says nothing about Alt. The matches() helper added with the Alt bindings
compared meta, so the default { key: "escape" } binding never matched and the
dismiss branch was unreachable. meta is now ignored for escape specifically.

Accepting on Enter immediately produced a new menu, so the second Enter accepted
that instead of submitting and the line could never be run. The menu now stays
shut until the next keystroke — a space counts. Not time-based: a timer either
expires while you are still deciding or holds the menu back after you have
carried on typing, and neither is the condition that matters.

sortMethod gains "lastUsed": most recently used first, for every suggestion
type. Distinct from "recency", which reproduces Q's 50-75 promotion band and so
barely moves an option (priority 45) even once it has been used.
